            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">I know a lot of us have mixed feelings about the events reference, because it simply isn't supposed to be here. I'm merging everything into a single guide article, and next I will fix the broken anchors within in it (the current state gives me no appetite to modify this page).</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40443",
            "title": "Move Events reference as one article under DOM API",
            "date_modified": "2025-07-20T06:37:59.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-07-19T14:56:55.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Josh-Cena",
                "url": "https://github.com/Josh-Cena"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/576623?u=88392c52422628facfd7cf108241d2864680915d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Add interactive examples to <code class=\"notranslate\">sin()</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">cos()</code> CSS functions.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">On September 2025, both <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/sin\" rel=\"nofollow\">sin()</a> and <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/cos\" rel=\"nofollow\">cos()</a> will become <a href=\"https://web.dev/baseline\" rel=\"nofollow\">baseline widely available</a>, yet both MDN articles have minimal information about the functions.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The interactive examples interface enhances the learning experience by allowing visitors to modify the code and see the results. This is a more instructive way to understand how these CSS functions work.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related pull requests</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1324227543\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/19016\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/19016/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/19016\">#19016</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1327573895\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/19119\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/19119/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/19119\">#19119</a></li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40441",
            "title": "Add interactive examples to `sin()` and `cos()` CSS functions",
            "date_modified": "2025-07-19T16:01:30.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-07-19T09:54:37.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "ramiy",
                "url": "https://github.com/ramiy"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23019147?u=4c0de81596ced64dc067dea5686f7ca2912db0cb&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Changes the phrasing to follow this approach: \"matches {what} when a user {action}\".</li>\n<li>Removes \"but does not necessarily activate it\" because it's not very clear and can cause confusion. This idea is also being explained in the next sentence.</li>\n<li>spells out \"activate\" as \"pressing the mouse button\" in the second sentence.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I came across this page randomly and noticed a scope to improve for clarity.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40429",
            "title": "fix(css): Improve description of `:hover` pseudo-class",
            "date_modified": "2025-07-18T15:38:17.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-07-18T15:36:17.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "dipikabh",
